## 0. Acceptance

This is a proprietary license agreement. Redeeming a key, downloading, extracting, installing, running, or otherwise using the Kit constitutes full acceptance of these terms. If you do not agree, do not download or use the Kit.

The license is non-exclusive, royalty-free, worldwide, and lasts for the full term of the exclusive right.

## 1. Definition

**The Kit** means VibeOS in its entirety and in all its parts: the software and accompanying materials, including but not limited to rules and working standards, skills, hooks, templates, documentation, guides, the wiki, the second-brain protocol, and **RepoBrain** (the repository brain — the code indexer and all its components).

Everything delivered to you in the `vibeos-kit-<version>.tar.gz` archive is the Kit. The exact contents of a delivery are defined by `tools/build-kit/kit.manifest`.

Each part of the Kit — every skill, every rule, RepoBrain, the wiki, the documentation — is protected in its own right. Using any part is governed by this agreement just as using the whole.

**The Kit is not what you build with it.** Your code, your product, your notes, and your plans are not the Kit and are not covered by this agreement.

## 1a. The key

Your access key is issued to you personally and carries a limited number of activations.

You may **not** transfer, publish, sell, or provide the key to third parties — neither the key itself nor the download link obtained with it. Transferring a key is equivalent to transferring the Kit (Section 3.2).

Download links are temporary and intended for you alone.

## 2. Permitted

**2.1.** Use the Kit to build your own projects, in any number, including commercial ones.

**2.2.** Release, publish, sell, and distribute the **product** you build with the Kit — a deployed application, site, service, or build. The rights holder claims no rights to your code, your product, or your revenue.

**2.3.** Install the Kit on your own devices and in your own private repositories, without limit.

**2.4.** Modify the Kit for your own use, including filling in templates and adapting rules and skills to your project.

## 3. Prohibited

**3.1. Publishing the Kit's files publicly** — original or modified. This includes public repositories (**including a repository of your own project, if the Kit's files are in it**), file hosting, torrents, public package registries, open chats or channels, and publications reproducing the files in full.

**3.2.** Transferring the Kit to third parties, in whole or in part, for free or for a fee.

**3.3.** Selling, reselling, renting, sublicensing the Kit, or offering access to it as a service.

**3.4.** Creating derivative products intended for distribution: another kit, template, starter, skill set, or competing product.

**3.5.** Removing or altering authorship notices or this agreement.

**3.6.** Circumventing technical protection or access-control measures.

Any right not expressly granted in Section 2 is reserved.

## 4. Open-sourcing your own project

To publish your project's source code, **remove the Kit's files from the published copy** (see Section 1). Everything else is yours and may be published freely. Section 3.1 restricts publishing the Kit, not you.

## 5. Breach

If you exceed the rights granted, the rights holder may unilaterally terminate this agreement in whole or in part. Upon termination, your right to use the Kit ends and the Kit must be deleted.

**Products created before termination remain yours** — Section 2.2 survives termination.

## 6. No warranty, no liability

The Kit is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or implied, including fitness for a particular purpose, absence of errors, or uninterrupted operation. The rights holder is not liable for any direct or indirect damages, including data loss and lost profits.

**The Kit drives an AI agent that writes code and runs commands on your machines.** You are responsible for what reaches your product, your repository, and your server.

## 7. Third-party components

Some parts of the Kit were not created by the rights holder and are distributed under their own licenses. **This agreement does not apply to them and does not restrict them** — your rights under those licenses stand independently of Sections 2 and 3.

As of version 1.0:

| Component | Rights holder | License |
|---|---|---|
| `.claude/skills/frontend-design/` | Anthropic | Apache-2.0 (`LICENSE.txt` included) |
| `.claude/skills/skill-creator/` | Anthropic | Apache-2.0 (`LICENSE.txt` included) |

In addition, RepoBrain and other parts of the Kit rely on external libraries installed by a package manager at install time (MIT, Apache-2.0, Unlicense, and others). These are not part of the distribution and are used under their own terms.

All other parts of the Kit — the rules, the remaining skills, hooks, templates, documentation, the wiki, the second-brain protocol, and the RepoBrain source — were created by the rights holder and are governed by Sections 2 and 3.

## 8. Governing law

The laws of the Russian Federation.

